1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:07,216
Twenty miles northwest of Sarajevo, above the small Bosnian town of Visoko, there is a hill.

2
00:00:07,216 --> 00:00:10,358
Steep, forested, and strangely triangular.

3
00:00:10,358 --> 00:00:13,800
From the right angle, it looks like a pyramid.

4
00:00:14,266 --> 00:00:23,263
In October two thousand and five, a Bosnian-American businessman from Houston, Semir Osmanagić, announced that it was one.

5
00:00:23,263 --> 00:00:24,664
Not just a pyramid.

6
00:00:24,664 --> 00:00:29,899
The largest and oldest on Earth, bigger than the Great Pyramid of Giza.

7
00:00:30,366 --> 00:00:32,302
Concrete stronger than ours.

8
00:00:32,302 --> 00:00:34,100
Tunnels running for miles.

9
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:37,627
An energy beam shooting from the summit into space.

10
00:00:37,627 --> 00:00:43,366
Builders tens of thousands of years old and, in some tellings, help from the stars.

11
00:00:43,833 --> 00:00:46,869
Hundreds of thousands of visitors have come.

12
00:00:46,869 --> 00:00:51,975
So today, we treat this hill like any building that wants official papers.

13
00:00:51,975 --> 00:00:53,700
We send in the inspector.

14
00:00:54,166 --> 00:00:55,455
Seven inspections.

15
00:00:55,455 --> 00:00:58,247
Every item passes or fails on evidence.

16
00:00:58,247 --> 00:01:02,399
At the end, we sign the certificate, and give the verdict.

17
00:01:06,866 --> 00:01:09,331
Inspection one: the site survey.

18
00:01:09,331 --> 00:01:13,183
The so-called Pyramid of the Sun is Visočica hill.

19
00:01:13,183 --> 00:01:17,574
It rises a little over two hundred metres above the town.

20
00:01:17,574 --> 00:01:24,200
Across the valley, Osmanagić named a second hill, Plješevica, the Pyramid of the Moon.

21
00:01:24,666 --> 00:01:30,855
He added a Pyramid of the Dragon, a Pyramid of Love, and a Temple of Mother Earth.

22
00:01:30,855 --> 00:01:37,799
Sun and Moon were borrowed from Mexico's Teotihuacan, where real pyramids carry those names.

23
00:01:38,266 --> 00:01:48,425
In April two thousand and five, he says, he looked at the hill, checked a compass, and saw triangular faces turned to north, south, east and west.

24
00:01:48,425 --> 00:01:51,000
Nature, he decided, does not do that.

25
00:01:51,466 --> 00:01:54,923
A surveyor later called the orientation perfect.

26
00:01:54,923 --> 00:02:05,366
But geologist Robert Schoch of Boston University, who flew over the valley in two thousand and six, saw natural hills, not a four-sided building.

27
00:02:05,833 --> 00:02:10,128
Geologists have a name for triangular hills: flatirons.

28
00:02:10,128 --> 00:02:16,219
A hard, tilted rock layer over softer rock, worn into a steep triangular face.

29
00:02:16,219 --> 00:02:22,233
They are common worldwide, from Colorado to Russia's so-called twin pyramids.

30
00:02:22,699 --> 00:02:29,852
Tuzla geologist Sejfudin Vrabac counted dozens of similar landforms in this basin alone.

31
00:02:29,852 --> 00:02:37,166
A pyramid shape, as archaeologist Curtis Runnels notes, is a form nature makes, and keeps.

32
00:02:37,633 --> 00:02:42,071
Osmanagić announced an international group of archaeologists.

33
00:02:42,071 --> 00:02:48,764
Many of those named said they had never agreed to take part, and had never been to the site.

34
00:02:48,764 --> 00:02:53,566
A promised Oxford archaeologist turned out to be an undergraduate.

35
00:02:54,033 --> 00:02:58,455
Survey result: a real shape, but one nature makes all the time.

36
00:02:58,455 --> 00:03:00,000
So we look underneath.

37
00:03:00,466 --> 00:03:03,207
Inspection two: the ground report.

38
00:03:03,207 --> 00:03:08,769
Ironically, the first test was ordered by Osmanagić's own foundation.

39
00:03:08,769 --> 00:03:16,266
In early two thousand and six, geologists from the University of Tuzla drilled into Visočica.

40
00:03:16,733 --> 00:03:19,836
Six boreholes, three to seventeen metres deep.

41
00:03:19,836 --> 00:03:30,833
Their verdict, in May two thousand and six: a natural formation, built of layered sediments, conglomerate, clay and sandstone, the same as the mountains around it.

42
00:03:31,300 --> 00:03:33,966
That fits the valley's known history.

43
00:03:33,966 --> 00:03:42,903
About ten million years ago, as the mountains of central Bosnia rose, this valley flooded into a lake some forty miles long.

44
00:03:42,903 --> 00:03:47,300
Rivers poured gravel, sand and mud into it, layer upon layer.

45
00:03:47,766 --> 00:03:49,740
Quiet years left thin clay.

46
00:03:49,740 --> 00:03:54,784
Floods dumped thick beds of gravel, which hardened into conglomerate.

47
00:03:54,784 --> 00:04:00,633
Later, tectonic forces tilted and cracked the old lake floor into angular hills.

48
00:04:01,099 --> 00:04:03,327
Schoch noticed something else.

49
00:04:03,327 --> 00:04:07,635
The sandstone layers repeat at intervals of about a metre.

50
00:04:07,635 --> 00:04:08,600
Regular, yes.

51
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:12,462
But geologists have a word for that too: cyclothems.

52
00:04:12,462 --> 00:04:15,433
Natural, repeating cycles of deposition.

53
00:04:15,900 --> 00:04:20,954
Osmanagić's answer: beneath the soil is not rock, but a construction.

54
00:04:20,954 --> 00:04:29,233
His foundation dates the soil on top to twelve to fifteen thousand years, so whatever lies beneath must be older.

55
00:04:29,699 --> 00:04:34,705
Ground report: the same lake-bed layers as every other hill in the basin.

56
00:04:34,705 --> 00:04:36,899
So what about the famous blocks?

57
00:04:37,366 --> 00:04:39,358
Inspection three: the walls.

58
00:04:39,358 --> 00:04:42,843
In April two thousand and six, the digging began.

59
00:04:42,843 --> 00:04:48,249
Within days, crews uncovered large, flat-faced stone blocks on the hillside.

60
00:04:48,249 --> 00:04:53,300
The headline went around the world: experts find evidence of a pyramid.

61
00:04:53,766 --> 00:05:01,222
The claim: these are concrete blocks, cast on site by a lost civilisation, harder than modern concrete.

62
00:05:01,222 --> 00:05:08,100
The foundation calls it a geopolymer, with strength up to a hundred and fifty-five megapascals.

63
00:05:08,566 --> 00:05:11,640
Schoch spent ten days on the site that summer.

64
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:22,199
Where the team saw poured concrete, he saw natural conglomerate and sandstone, broken into blocks by tectonic stress and by the hill slowly slumping downhill.

65
00:05:22,666 --> 00:05:26,834
The decisive clue: block size matches layer thickness.

66
00:05:26,834 --> 00:05:33,240
Thin sandstone beds broke into small slabs, thick conglomerate into massive blocks.

67
00:05:33,240 --> 00:05:35,633
Exactly what natural rock does.

68
00:05:36,100 --> 00:05:43,033
A geologist invited by the team hailed the blocks, then called his own results inconclusive.

69
00:05:43,033 --> 00:05:51,699
Anthony Harding, head of the European Association of Archaeologists, examined the same blocks: entirely geological.

70
00:05:52,166 --> 00:06:01,300
On the Pyramid of the Moon, flat sandstone plates separated by clay became paved terraces: the steps of a giant stepped pyramid.

71
00:06:01,766 --> 00:06:07,925
But Schoch says workers carved the hillside between natural layers to create the steps.

72
00:06:07,925 --> 00:06:15,500
Archaeologist Brian Stewart warned the hills were being sculpted, stripping away real medieval archaeology.

73
00:06:15,966 --> 00:06:24,333
Walls result: natural rock, broken the way natural rock breaks, and steps made, at least in part, by the excavation itself.

74
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:27,019
Inspection four: the basement.

75
00:06:27,019 --> 00:06:36,265
Near the village of Ravne, the foundation opened a tunnel it calls part of a vast prehistoric labyrinth linking the pyramids.

76
00:06:36,265 --> 00:06:39,224
First two point four miles were claimed.

77
00:06:39,224 --> 00:06:41,000
Now, tens of kilometres.

78
00:06:41,466 --> 00:06:52,266
In two thousand and nine, journalist Colin Woodard crawled in: a cramped passage, about three feet high, cut through loose, unconsolidated sand and pebbles.

79
00:06:52,733 --> 00:06:57,524
Schoch had found a tunnel clearly entered and changed in recent times.

80
00:06:57,524 --> 00:07:04,233
Collapsed ceilings, graffiti, and local stories that the Yugoslav army had once used tunnels here.

81
00:07:04,699 --> 00:07:10,188
Then the inscriptions: symbols on boulders, presented as ancient writing.

82
00:07:10,188 --> 00:07:18,008
A former foundation geologist told a Bosnian magazine there were no marks when she first saw the stones.

83
00:07:18,008 --> 00:07:19,962
Later, she saw fresh cuts.

84
00:07:19,962 --> 00:07:21,466
Osmanagić denies it.

85
00:07:21,933 --> 00:07:32,066
Today the tunnels are a wellness attraction: negative ions, meditation sessions, and published healing testimonials, from sinus trouble to tumours.

86
00:07:32,533 --> 00:07:34,131
Negative ions are real.

87
00:07:34,131 --> 00:07:38,646
Damp air near running water is rich in them, in caves everywhere.

88
00:07:38,646 --> 00:07:47,399
But a tunnel through gravel still needs a date and a digger, and no independent study has yet established who dug it, or when.

89
00:07:47,866 --> 00:07:53,040
Basement result: real tunnels, recently modified, origin unproven.

90
00:07:53,040 --> 00:07:56,333
Now, the claim that made this hill famous.

91
00:07:56,800 --> 00:07:58,940
Inspection five: the wiring.

92
00:07:58,940 --> 00:08:09,263
In two thousand and ten, a team led by Croatian physicist Slobodan Mizdrak reported ultrasound on the summit of the Pyramid of the Sun.

93
00:08:09,263 --> 00:08:12,933
A steady signal at about twenty-eight kilohertz.

94
00:08:13,399 --> 00:08:17,763
Then, a beam four and a half metres wide rising from the top.

95
00:08:17,763 --> 00:08:20,838
A drone flight in two thousand and sixteen.

96
00:08:20,838 --> 00:08:27,133
Even a metal plate, deep underground, said to generate more than ten kilowatts of power.

97
00:08:27,600 --> 00:08:31,870
Osmanagić calls it Tesla's scalar waves, faster than light.

98
00:08:31,870 --> 00:08:35,779
A cosmic internet for communication across the galaxy.

99
00:08:35,779 --> 00:08:39,543
From there it is a short step to the alien question.

100
00:08:39,543 --> 00:08:42,366
Who would need a transmitter like that?

101
00:08:42,833 --> 00:08:46,988
Twenty-eight kilohertz is ultrasound, above human hearing.

102
00:08:46,988 --> 00:08:55,799
Ordinary things make it: insects, bats, wind in leaves, electronic power supplies, and sometimes the measuring gear itself.

103
00:08:56,266 --> 00:09:06,166
A real beam would be easy to confirm: independent teams, calibrated instruments, control hills nearby, results physicists can check.

104
00:09:06,166 --> 00:09:12,466
The main write-up, posted in twenty twenty-five, is a preprint by Osmanagić himself.

105
00:09:12,933 --> 00:09:14,440
And faster than light?

106
00:09:14,440 --> 00:09:17,045
That one fails before any measurement.

107
00:09:17,045 --> 00:09:21,636
No signal carrying information has ever been shown to outrun light.

108
00:09:21,636 --> 00:09:26,433
It would break relativity, one of the best-tested theories in physics.

109
00:09:26,899 --> 00:09:32,399
Wiring result: an unreplicated signal, and no alien fingerprint anywhere.

110
00:09:32,866 --> 00:09:34,908
Inspection six: the date stamp.

111
00:09:34,908 --> 00:09:36,620
Every building has a date.

112
00:09:36,620 --> 00:09:38,266
This one has had several.

113
00:09:38,733 --> 00:09:43,449
In two thousand and six, Osmanagić spoke of twelve thousand years.

114
00:09:43,449 --> 00:09:50,808
By twenty twelve, radiocarbon on a leaf found on a block gave twenty-four thousand eight hundred years.

115
00:09:50,808 --> 00:09:52,666
Then twenty-nine thousand.

116
00:09:52,666 --> 00:09:54,666
Later, thirty-four thousand.

117
00:09:55,133 --> 00:09:57,163
The problem is what was dated.

118
00:09:57,163 --> 00:09:58,651
A leaf dates the leaf.

119
00:09:58,651 --> 00:10:05,688
Plant remains on or between rock layers tell you when the plant lived, not that anyone built the layers.

120
00:10:05,688 --> 00:10:10,966
And Schoch found real fossil leaves in these sediments, millions of years old.

121
00:10:11,433 --> 00:10:14,588
Now picture Europe thirty thousand years ago.

122
00:10:14,588 --> 00:10:17,953
The Ice Age was heading toward its coldest peak.

123
00:10:17,953 --> 00:10:21,668
People lived in small bands of hunters and gatherers.

124
00:10:21,668 --> 00:10:27,066
Farming, towns and metal were all still more than twenty thousand years away.

125
00:10:27,533 --> 00:10:31,875
Curtis Runnels, an expert on the prehistoric Balkans, is blunt.

126
00:10:31,875 --> 00:10:37,251
Those people did not have the tools or the skills for monumental architecture.

127
00:10:37,251 --> 00:10:43,799
Cultures able to build big structures appear here only about two and a half thousand years ago.

128
00:10:44,266 --> 00:10:45,409
So who built it?

129
00:10:45,409 --> 00:10:50,693
Osmanagić's wider writings answer: a civilisation more advanced than ours.

130
00:10:50,693 --> 00:11:00,333
Elsewhere he has written that the Maya came from the Pleiades by way of Atlantis, and that humans are a product of genetic engineering.

131
00:11:00,799 --> 00:11:05,885
Date stamp: no workshops, no tools, no bones, no hearths, no builders.

132
00:11:05,885 --> 00:11:07,484
Just leaves in layers.

133
00:11:07,484 --> 00:11:10,100
So who really did live on this hill?

134
00:11:10,566 --> 00:11:13,374
Inspection seven: the real tenants.

135
00:11:13,374 --> 00:11:25,166
On the summit lie the ruins of Visoki, a royal castle town of medieval Bosnia, first named in a charter of Tvrtko the First in thirteen fifty-five.

136
00:11:25,633 --> 00:11:29,442
Documents were issued there until fourteen thirty-six.

137
00:11:29,442 --> 00:11:40,233
And the castle sat on older layers: a Roman lookout post and, beneath it, traces of settlement that Schoch says may reach back about five thousand years.

138
00:11:40,700 --> 00:11:47,135
In two thousand and eight, independent archaeologists found medieval artefacts on the hill.

139
00:11:47,135 --> 00:11:54,066
Bosnia's monuments commission widened the protected zone, pushing the pyramid digs off the summit.

140
00:11:54,533 --> 00:12:09,200
In December two thousand and six, leading European archaeologists signed a declaration calling the project a cruel hoax on an unsuspecting public, and a waste of resources needed to protect genuine heritage.

141
00:12:09,666 --> 00:12:18,066
Historian Garrett Fagan of Penn State compared it to letting someone bulldoze Stonehenge in search of secret chambers underneath.

142
00:12:18,533 --> 00:12:20,275
Why did so many believe?

143
00:12:20,275 --> 00:12:25,431
Bosnia was emerging from the war of nineteen ninety-two to ninety-five.

144
00:12:25,431 --> 00:12:27,681
Visoko itself had been shelled.

145
00:12:27,681 --> 00:12:33,200
A story of great ancestors, and of a brighter future, was powerful medicine.

146
00:12:33,666 --> 00:12:39,510
Officials embraced it, including a prime minister and members of the presidency.

147
00:12:39,510 --> 00:12:44,259
Critics, Smithsonian reported, were shouted down as anti-Bosnian.

148
00:12:44,259 --> 00:12:45,866
Some received threats.

149
00:12:46,333 --> 00:12:51,997
And the town did gain something real: tourists, souvenir stalls, a park, jobs.

150
00:12:51,997 --> 00:12:57,733
Many people in Visoko are glad of the visitors, whatever the hills are made of.

151
00:12:58,200 --> 00:13:02,904
Tenants: medieval kings, Roman soldiers, Neolithic villagers.

152
00:13:02,904 --> 00:13:06,529
Real history, sitting on top of a natural hill.

153
00:13:06,529 --> 00:13:08,766
Time to sign the certificate.

154
00:13:09,233 --> 00:13:10,980
The inspection is complete.

155
00:13:10,980 --> 00:13:12,533
Here is the certificate.

156
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:17,708
Made of the same lake-bed layers as the hills around it: evidence.

157
00:13:17,708 --> 00:13:21,489
Blocks broken to match the layer thickness: evidence.

158
00:13:21,489 --> 00:13:25,127
Medieval and Roman remains on the summit: evidence.

159
00:13:25,127 --> 00:13:28,266
Steps carved by the digs themselves: likely.

160
00:13:28,733 --> 00:13:34,455
The world's largest pyramid, twelve to thirty-four thousand years old: debunked.

161
00:13:34,455 --> 00:13:39,247
A twenty-eight kilohertz energy beam with alien links: no evidence.

162
00:13:39,247 --> 00:13:42,966
And who dug the Ravne tunnels, and when: still open.

163
00:13:43,433 --> 00:13:44,416
The verdict.

164
00:13:44,416 --> 00:13:52,937
The Bosnian pyramids are natural hills: flatirons of ancient lake sediments, tilted and worn by geology.

165
00:13:52,937 --> 00:13:53,839
No pyramid.

166
00:13:53,839 --> 00:13:56,297
No Ice Age super-civilisation.

167
00:13:56,297 --> 00:13:58,100
No cosmic transmitter.

168
00:13:58,566 --> 00:14:00,399
The blocks are broken rock.

169
00:14:00,399 --> 00:14:05,219
The steps were, in part, made with shovels after two thousand and five.

170
00:14:05,219 --> 00:14:08,003
The dates come from leaves, not builders.

171
00:14:08,003 --> 00:14:11,533
And the beam has never been independently confirmed.

172
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:25,100
What stays open is smaller, and more honest: the true history of the Ravne tunnels, and what the valley's real archaeology, from the Neolithic to medieval Visoki, still has to tell.

173
00:14:25,566 --> 00:14:28,712
The real wonder of Visoko is not a pyramid.

174
00:14:28,712 --> 00:14:39,102
It is a hill that holds ten million years of an ancient lake, the ruins of a royal town, and a people who badly wanted their past to be great.

175
00:14:39,102 --> 00:14:40,199
It already was.

176
00:14:40,666 --> 00:14:42,535
That is the inspection report.

177
00:14:42,535 --> 00:14:44,901
Would you have signed the certificate?

178
00:14:44,901 --> 00:14:50,133
Tell us in the comments, and subscribe for the next ancient mystery put to the test.
